{
	id: "016154E27B2079BE"
	group: "499A93482811AC21"
	order_index: 5
	filename: "casting_a_line"
	title: "Casting a Line"
	subtitle: ["MOD : Aquaculture 2"]
	default_quest_shape: ""
	default_hide_dependency_lines: false
	quests: [
		{
			title: "A Hobby and Life of Culture"
			x: 0.75d
			y: 1.0d
			shape: "square"
			subtitle: "MOD : Aquaculture 2"
			description: [
				"&3Well well, hello there Bandit. Name's Fishin' Fae, head researcher for the Aquatic Relics division. And yer about to ask about what kinda research one can get into for fishin, right? Well, lots. "
				""
				"&3See, the FOPGame Server has copied off my research for their little game-but-not-a-game, and given it the brand name Aquaculture. It's about the power of the seas, that one can only harness by mastering the rod, the fish, and the eye of the storm that is fishing."
				""
				"&3Before anything, though, yer gonna need to make yourself a few basic things. First is an Iron Fishing Rod, it's a bit better than the regular wooden Fishing Rod, and ya can add special things to it. Like an Iron Hook, as an example."
				""
				"&3Also, make a Worm Farm. It works kinda like the Composter: put in raw food and plant matter, then Right Click with an empty hand to get out Worms!"
			]
			dependencies: ["1D0853ADC7295AEB"]
			id: "726BE272AB161992"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "0F13699CFBB9AC75"
					type: "item"
					item: {
						id: "aquaculture:iron_fishing_rod"
						Count: 1b
						tag: {
							Damage: 0
						}
					}
				}
				{
					id: "3B4F3907A03681D1"
					type: "item"
					item: "aquaculture:iron_hook"
				}
				{
					id: "1815E93306836D4A"
					type: "item"
					item: "aquaculture:worm_farm"
				}
			]
			rewards: [{
				id: "4B6FC42F1ED70954"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Tackle and Carry"
			x: 2.25d
			y: 1.0d
			shape: "rsquare"
			description: [
				"&3A good fisher is one who can catch fish. A great fisher is one who can catch any fish, and knows what tools to use to do so. And there are tons of fish and tools to catch fish, which then you run into an issue of... how the heck do ya carry all that equipment?!"
				""
				"&3Well, the answer to that is simple. Take your tools(like your hooks) and your bait(like Worms), and put em in a Tackle Box!"
				""
				"&3Coincidentally, this is also how you attatch those tools to your Iron Fishing Rod (or better). Place down the Tackle Box, and Right Click it to open it up. Look at all that room for yer stuff!"
				""
				"&3On the left ya have storage for your hooks, your bait, your lines, and more. On the Right, ya can put your Fishing Rod to attach all those tools to your Rod."
				""
				"&3Then you can break your Tacklebox to pick it up. "
			]
			dependencies: ["726BE272AB161992"]
			id: "29661E8B057202C7"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "4C966272107345B0"
					type: "item"
					item: {
						id: "aquaculture:worm"
						Count: 1b
						tag: {
							Damage: 0
						}
					}
				}
				{
					id: "305189FEE6FBECC1"
					type: "item"
					item: "aquaculture:tackle_box"
				}
			]
			rewards: [{
				id: "3E436E99CA6F606C"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Filet O' Fish"
			x: 3.75d
			y: 1.0d
			shape: "rsquare"
			description: [
				"&3Now, fishing with these Aquaculture rods is just like normal rods. Except only Aquaculture Rods can catch certain fish... and certain not-fish."
				""
				"&3Once you catch some fish, you could use em like normal fish in recipes that call for fish. Or you can use a Fillet Knife on em to slice em into some nice, clean filets."
				""
				"&3Though I must say, the FOPGame Server doesn't have much you can turn the filets into. You can cook em as is, or you can make Sushi with em!"
				""
				"&3Though, the bosses would definitely say thats more than enough. Between the two of us, let's just say they may like Sushi a bit."
			]
			dependencies: ["29661E8B057202C7"]
			id: "7FC2234EEA487630"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "4D086991AE830AC9"
					type: "item"
					item: {
						id: "aquaculture:wooden_fillet_knife"
						Count: 1b
						tag: {
							Damage: 0
						}
					}
				}
				{
					id: "71C878996B83B119"
					type: "item"
					item: "aquaculture:fish_fillet_raw"
				}
				{
					id: "32542070AD1EBEC8"
					type: "item"
					item: "aquaculture:sushi"
				}
			]
			rewards: [{
				id: "721B02B08832107A"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Trash or Treasure"
			x: 5.25d
			y: 1.0d
			shape: "rsquare"
			description: [
				"&3Now, I mentioned not-fish, yer right. And that's where another part of my research comes in, Bandit."
				""
				"&3Now, yer probably thinking that things like this Box here are just discarded trash from other Users, yeah? And you'd be... partially right. In the Real World, there's some odd magic that can happen with these containers you can fish up. Sometimes... they contain treasure. Treasure that was not part of the trash originally, it just... magically appeared."
				""
				"&3The FOPGame Server replicates this mysterious magical treasure occurance. The more intricate the 'trash' box you fish up, the higher the chance of treasure being inside."
				""
				"&3Ye gotta admit its a good incentive to go fishing in the game."
			]
			dependencies: ["7FC2234EEA487630"]
			id: "61F3F6680887946E"
			tasks: [{
				id: "24B21085B6E63450"
				type: "item"
				item: "aquaculture:box"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "2262345C6DED1B64"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Give It Your Style"
			x: 2.25d
			y: -0.5d
			shape: "rsquare"
			description: [
				"&3Ye probably noticed that your fishing pole has a few extra attachment points in the Tackle Box, yeah? Well, those are for customizing yer stuff."
				""
				"&3Specifically, ye can customize your Fishing Line and Bobber."
				""
				"&3These don't make ya fish any better, mind. But yer able to dye both of these like Leather Armor: Combine em with any number of Dyes in a Crafting Table."
			]
			dependencies: ["29661E8B057202C7"]
			id: "0B2AC4B5593F275B"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "5473248A961317B4"
					type: "item"
					item: "aquaculture:fishing_line"
				}
				{
					id: "1E1A3C0AB78D9905"
